<title>USA: Airport Systems gets Swiss contract.</title>
<headline>Airport Systems gets Swiss contract.</headline>
<dateline>OVERLAND PARK, Kan. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airport Systems International Inc said Thursday it was awarded a fixed-price contract with Swisscontrol to supply its Model 8000 Differential Global Positioning System (DGPS) ground station for the airport at Lugano, Switzerland.</p>
<p>Terms were not announced.  The company said this is its initial sale of a DGPS ground station.</p>
<p>An interim ground station was installed at Lugano in October, 1995, it added.</p>
<p>Airport Systems manufactures, markets and installs ground-based equipment and airfield signs.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
